  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "If two triangles have two pairs of equal sides and one pair of equal angles, are they necessarily congruent?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "They are necessarily congruent",
    "B": "Not necessarily; the angle must be the included angle between the two sides",
    "C": "They are necessarily not congruent",
    "D": "They are necessarily congruent by SSA"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "SAS requires the equal angles to be the included angles between the two sides. If the angles are opposite one of the sides (SSA), congruence is not guaranteed.",
